<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1989">1989</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as APEC</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation is an intergovernmental forum of 21 Pacific Rim economies founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canberra">Canberra</a> in 1989 at the initiative of the Australian prime minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bob-hawke">Bob Hawke</a>. It promotes free trade and economic integration in the region through annual leaders' meetings and agreed goals, and its members include the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asia-pacific-economic-cooperation.jpg" alt="Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cflm001 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Asia-Pacific_Economic_Cooperation_nations.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
